{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The young of your cattle.</b> The offspring of your cattle — what the female casts from her womb." "<b>And the flocks of your sheep.</b> Menachem explained ״אַבִּירֵי בָשָׁ״ן (Psalms 22) as the choicest of the flock, like ״בְּעַשְׁתְּרֹת קַרְנַיִם״ (Genesis 14) — a term of strength. And Onkelos translates ״וְעֶדְרֵי עָנָךְ.״ And our Sages said: why is their name עַשְׁתָּרוֹת? Because they enrich their owners (Ḥullin 4)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:17.628014287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}